from lib import *
U='b2-boliviaaltiplano'
chall('bolivia-altiplano',{
f'{U}-01':C('The Lake That Keeps the Frost Away','You are Meg. You and Carlos are watching a documentary about Lake Titicaca, and he asks why families can grow crops by the lake.','Tell Carlos which families can grow potatoes and barley, and why.',['Say who can grow potatoes','Say that the lake softens the frosts'],'Las familias que viven cerca del lago pueden cultivar papa porque el agua suaviza las heladas.','The families who live near the lake can grow potatoes because the water softens the frosts.','I can describe the high plateau and Lake Titicaca with relative clauses introduced by *que* and *quien*.'),
f'{U}-02':C('The Mint Is Now a Museum','You are Carlos. You and Meg are planning a trip to Potosí, and she asks what is left of the Mint.','Tell Meg what the Mint of Potosí is today.',['Say that the Mint is a museum now','Say what it was used for'],'Hoy la Casa de la Moneda está convertida en museo, y allí se acuñaban monedas de plata.','Today the Mint is turned into a museum, and silver coins were minted there.','I can say what Potosí looks like today with *estar* + participle.'),
f'{U}-03':C('Not a District, a City','You are Meg. You and Carlos are reading an article about La Paz and El Alto, and he thinks El Alto is a district of La Paz.','Correct Carlos: El Alto is not a district.',['Reject the idea that it is a district','Say what El Alto really is'],'No es que El Alto sea un barrio de La Paz, sino que es una ciudad con su propio gobierno.','It is not that El Alto is a district of La Paz; it is a city with its own government.','I can correct a wrong idea about La Paz and El Alto with *no es que… sino que…*.'),
f'{U}-04':C('What the Government Says About Coca','You are Carlos. You and Meg are preparing a talk about the coca leaf, and she asks what the Bolivian government says.','Tell Meg the government\'s position, naming the source.',['Name who says it','Say that coca is not cocaine'],'El gobierno boliviano dice que la coca tiene usos tradicionales y que no es cocaína.','The Bolivian government says that coca has traditional uses and that it is not cocaine.','I can say who says what about the coca leaf, using *según* and *dice que*.'),
f'{U}-05':C('However Much It Is Discussed','You are Meg. You and Carlos are watching a talk about the Constitution of 2009, and he asks which languages it recognises.','Tell Carlos the languages are official in spite of the debate.',['Grant that Spanish is spoken in the cities','Say that the indigenous languages are official too'],'Por más que se hable castellano en las ciudades, los idiomas indígenas también son oficiales.','However much Spanish is spoken in the cities, the indigenous languages are official too.','I can grant a point and still state my main idea with *por más que* + subjunctive.'),
f'{U}-consolidation':C('The Bolivian Highlands in Review','You are Carlos. You and Meg are preparing a short talk about the Bolivian highlands, and she asks where Titicaca lies.','Tell Meg which lake Bolivia shares with Peru.',['Name the lake','Say which country shares it'],'El lago Titicaca es el lago que Bolivia comparte con Perú.','Lake Titicaca is the lake that Bolivia shares with Peru.','I can review what I learned about the Bolivian highlands, from Lake Titicaca to the Constitution of 2009.')})
